\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Richard \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Stettiner\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Die illustrierten Prudentiushandschriften, Bd. 1: Textband. Berlin 1895, S. 32. \endash  Helen \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Woodruff\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , The illustrated manuscripts of Prudentius. Cambridge 1930. Abb. 120. \endash  Francis \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Wormald\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , English drawings of the tenth and eleventh centuries. London 1952, S. 73. \endash  Neil R. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Ker\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Catalogue of manuscripts containing Anglo-Saxon. Oxford 1957, S. 347f. \endash  Adelheid \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Heimann, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Three Illustrations from the Bury St. Edmunds Psalter and their Prototypes. Notes on the Iconography of Some Anglo-Saxon Drawings. In: Journal of the Warburg and Courtauld Institutes 29, 1966, S. 46. \endash  Thomas H. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Ohlgren \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  (Hrsg.), Insular and Anglo-Saxon illustrated manuscripts. An iconic catalogue c. A.D. 625 to 1100 (Garland reference library to the humanities 631). New York / London 1986, Nr. 155. \endash  Sources of Anglo-Saxon literary culture: a trial version (Medieval & Renaissance texts and studies 74), hrsg. von Frederick M. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Biggs\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . New York 1990, S. 153. \endash  Kathleen M. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Openshaw\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Weapons in the daily battle. Images of the conquest of evil in the early medieval psalter. In: Art bulletin 75, 1993, S. 31. \endash  Mark \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Atherton\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , The image of the Temple in the \u8222 \'84Psychomachia\ldblquote  and Late Anglo-Saxon Literature. In: Bulletin of the John Rylands Library of Manchester 79/3, 1997, S. 265. \endash  Joachim \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Ott\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Krone und Kr\u246 \'f6nung: die Verhei\u223 \'dfung und Verleihung von Kronen in der Kunst von der Sp\u228 \'e4tantike bis um 1200 und die geistige Auslegung der Krone. Mainz 1998, S. 286. \endash  Gernot \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Wieland\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , Interpreting the Interpretation. The Polysemy of the Latin Gloss. In: The journal of Medieval Latin 8, 1998, S. 59, 63. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Hauke \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  2001, S. 315. \endash \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Brigit \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Ebersperger\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 , in: Angels\u228 \'e4chsisches Erbe in M\u252 \'fcnchen. Angels\u228 \'e4chsische Handschriften, Schreiber und Autoren aus den Best\u228 \'e4nden der Bayerischen Staatsbibliothek in M\u252 \'fcnchen, hrsg. von Hans \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Sauer\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . Frankfurt am Main 2005, S. 19, 38f. (Kat. 3). \endash  Gale R. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 Owen Crocker, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  Working with Anglo Saxon Manuscripts (Exeter medieval texts and studies). Exeter 2009, S. 148f. }

